{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks","id":874976,"title":"1001 Beast Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T16:14:45-07:00","id":874976,"title":"1001 Beast Story Hooks","content":"So, I figured all the other game lines have one of these, so why not finish the set? Anyway, just post whatever comes to mind!<br /> <br /> 1)The Brood has been dealing with an old, cunning Hero, one who's killed dozens of Beasts with disturbing ease. So it might come as a surprise when they arrive near the Brood's local haunts and peacefully approaches them. The Hero looks even crazier than normal, but their eyes are not filled with hate so much as... is that <i>regret?</i> <br /> <br /> If the Brood talks to the Hero, they'll try to beg forgiveness, claiming that &quot;the angels&quot; took them up to heaven to show them the wickedness of their ways, and so that the Hero might sign again the Book of Life and repent. In case any of the players decide to try on a hunch, they'll find the Hero is now Kin (a Mage, if they know that particular &quot;flavor&quot;). Now the Brood has a dilemma on their hands. Will vengeance and justice take charge, or will the Ex-Hero's apparently genuine remorse and the bonds of family demand mercy? <br /> <br /> 1A) As 1), but the Hero was also part of a band, who is now conveying to slaughter their traitorous &quot;friend&quot;. Will the Brood leave the Ex-Hero to their fate, or will they put themselves at risk for someone who would have murdered them just a day ago?<br /> <br /> 2) Word has spread through the Hive of a strange young woman. A smiling, cheerful psychologist, a veritable saint, her presence actually numbs and sates the Hunger of the Begotten, a euphoric experience that leaves the affected Beasts docile and eager for more (her practice is practically booming with new patients). Of course, side effects include the fact that Children who experience this effect are effectively Gorged for a few hours afterwords, but it's not like a Hero is going to notice this and decide to use little Ms. St Martha Jr as bait to capture their prey, right?<br /> <br /> 3) One day, the Brood or one of its members ends up dropping by to check up on some Kin to find that they're acting oddly. The Vampire is walking around in sunlight, the purely carnivorous werewolf is eating tofu, and the Lucifuge member is cowering in fear from an attack by a supernatural being. If confronted on this, not only do they fail to realize their behavior is odd, they actually don't remember the Begotten... or more bizarrely, their former nature. &quot;Former&quot;, because any attempt to check their status reveals them as pure humans. Worse, this isn't an isolated incident; some force is running around town &quot;curing&quot; supernaturals of their nature and memories. Can they figure out what's going on and stop it? And what if some of their Kin <b>want</b> to be affected?<br /> <br /> 4) You know how a hungry Horror will go out hunting to satisfy itself? Yeah, things have started to go wonky in regards to that. There's still feeding going on, and strange dreams as a result, but they don't provide fear anymore. Instead, the chief emotion victims seem to exhibit is <i>rapture</i>, normal people morphing into swooning zealots. Already, small cults are beginning to spread like wildfire as the afflicted unite in the hopes of calling the attention of their &quot;gods&quot;, and the PCs won't have long to stay neutral on the subject. Will they attempt to nip this in the bud before things descend into anarchy, or will they seize their new callings as divinities? And of course, just because it's now creating cultists doesn't mean that the Horror's deprivations aren't still calling Heroes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:03:24-07:00","id":875539,"title":"","content":"I'll throw one in, this is the story I'm running now:<br /> <br /> 5) The characters have a vested interest in blending in as Kindred, both for social and feeding purposes. They've made some connections in the Unbound and are just barely known enough to have the best of both worlds. Suddenly they start noticing some of their unbound contacts disappearing. The Prince is rounding them up and interrogating them. Upon some further investigation the characters find that the Prince is afraid of something called a Malkov being in his city, but the symptoms sound a lot more like a Beast using a contagious Nightmare on kindred. If they just let it go the players will eventually be found out by the Prince and his men, but pursuing the problem would mean going up against another Beast. It could only get worse if the offending Beast was the self styled new Apex, hunting Kindred for sport.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:18:02-07:00","id":921790,"title":"","content":"6) One of your contacts in the local ecosystem has heard some whispers that some kind of Super-Hero has appeared. She's tapped into the Bright dream deeper than ever, and some people swear she was pulling some Sailor Moon shit. It'd be funny if she hadn't annihilated three Beasts already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:47:06-07:00","id":924246,"title":"","content":"Hi there! First post on the forums, so please let me know if I'm following good policy. To start off, I have three story hooks, with two inspired by popular media.<br /> <br /> <u><b>7) You Meddling Kids!</b></u><br /> The aftermath of some of your more... <i>creative</i> feedings has always drawn people - gawkers ready to build your legend or baffled cops, the occassional wild-eyed Hero. Now, however, your trail has been picked up by a group of amateur monster hunters. You'd classify these annoyingly persistent sleuths as Heroes except for two things. First, they haven't tried to kill you, and second, they are totally convinced that you are a <i>fake</i>. Even repeated use of Nightmares hasn't seemed to deter the investigators. Even if they're not actively malevolent, their prying might lead a Hero to you or to your Family in the city's supernatural underworld.<br /> <br /> <u><b>8) Helicopter Parenting</b></u><br /> <br /> You have a daughter: a perfectly normal, fully human daughter. Maybe she was conceived before your Devouring, or maybe after it. Right now, she's in grade school, dealing with the normal problems of a child. Do you step in and use your powers to scare away all the bullies and push slacking teachers back into line, or do you stay hands off?<br /> <br /> If you do dive into the world of your daughter's school, however, you notice that it's a perilous neutral zone between various supernatural factions. The son of a Changeling courtier grows up with a few wolf-bloods and the distant relation of an elder vampire. These children could be a catalyst for peace between the people of the shadows... or they may become pawns or casualties in bloody war games.<br /> <br /> <u><b>9) Thriller!</b></u><br /> You know the drill: The moon is up, the dead are rising all over town, and menacing the people you'd usually feed on yourself. Can you stop the zombie menace AND save your perfectly planned date night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:15:05-07:00","id":924514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvedulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=924246#post924246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>9) Thriller!</b></u><br /> You know the drill: The moon is up, the dead are rising all over town, and menacing the people you'd usually feed on yourself. Can you stop the zombie menace AND save your perfectly planned date night?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dancing is not optional, but mandatory. Hmm. New Nightmare &quot;So You Think You Can Dance?&quot; that disrupts movement, reduces defense, etc.?<br /> <br /> Oh, and welcome to the forums!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:47:48-07:00","id":924713,"title":"","content":"<u><b>10) The Corrupting Touch</b></u><br /> <br /> Something strange is happening to the local area's Begotten, or more precisely, to the targets of their feeding. Some people who are fed on by Beasts are changing, their bodies warping to reflect the Horror of the Beast that fed on them. A Namtaru whose Horror manifests as a massive horned rat might cause their greasy black or brown body hair to grow over their victim's bodies, faces becoming elongated and muscles twitchy. An Anakim whose Horror takes the form of a shambling mass of blood-soaked metal shards finds that his last meal has gone into hiding as weird metallic growths manifest under the skin.<br /> <br /> Making a bad situation worse, those who are warped by a Beast's Horror gain the ability to sense the presence of the Begotten, with a particularly strong connection to the monster with whom their condition originates. Beasts in your city are now gaining collections of weird hangers-on. Obsessed cultists, children trying to please their cruel creator gods, hating and loving the Begotten all at once. What will you do when even your gentle feedings may leave scars?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:46:41-07:00","id":942382,"title":"","content":"Hi, everybody! My first official post! Yay!<br /> <br /> Anyhow, onto business:<br /> <b>11/)A Covey of Giants:</b> An Anakim 'hecatonchieres' has come to town, and he's gunning to become Apex. He's of the Incarnate Inheritance, which is bad enough, but---he has, as allies, a neonate covey of Acolytes of the Circle of the Crone, who worship him as a masculine aspect of the Earthmother!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-02-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T00:34:29-07:00","id":942552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=942382#post942382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, everybody! My first official post! Yay!<br /> <br /> Anyhow, onto business:<br /> <b>11/)A Covey of Giants:</b> An Anakim 'hecatonchieres' has come to town, and he's gunning to become Apex. He's of the Incarnate Inheritance, which is bad enough, but---he has, as allies, a neonate covey of Acolytes of the Circle of the Crone, who worship him as a masculine aspect of the Earthmother!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to see someone new here! Welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T15:07:58-07:00","id":943027,"title":"","content":"12) An ancient and powerful Bahamatuan summons Ravagers worldwide to New York City, which he has promised to utterly destroy in an orgy of madness and violence as a gift to the Begotten. How can the children convince a demigod not to go through with it's promise, and what is it's motivation? Leviathans don't live long enough to become ancient and powerful by destroying cities without a very very good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:14:14-07:00","id":943330,"title":"","content":"13) One of your Kindred buddies has Embraced somebody. No big deal, he's getting old and the Prince gave him the thumbs up. The problem is, apparently he was related to another friend, a Werewolf, and has started manifesting trait of the Dead Wolf bloodline. The Pack wants him back, but his Sire's not interested. You have been dragged in to intermediate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T00:13:02-07:00","id":943465,"title":"","content":"14) You know that guy you fed on the other night, the one from that weird cult that's just sprung up? Turns out that he went to the demigod at the heart of the cult and told him what happened. Now he's after you, thinking that you're possessed by a Titanspawn. How are you going to convince him of what you are and to stop coming after you? Can you make a deal with him and his followers, or will you have to deal with a cult full of guys just as fanatical as a Hero with the backing of something that can call down goddamn Miracles? And the worst thing? In his mind, he's doing nothing less than good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:26:35-07:00","id":943673,"title":"","content":"15) The Way Forward: <br /> The Beasts in your brood and local hive are of an observant sort. They watch, they discuss, they listen and only occasionally intervene. To them the Dark Mother left you with a purpose, to shepherd you younger siblings toward a higher goal. That mentality has kept the Beasts in your area closely connected with many of the supernatural communities. But what happens when all of these communities come under attack at once? Kindred are found burnt to a crisp in the light of the moon. The Mage world is in an uproar as Paradox has spiraled suddenly past the point of being controlled. The Werewolves have disappeared into the shadow as mysterious and illusive spirits have begun a protracted war with the local ones. The Changelings are in disarray and panic when all of their senses tell them they've entered a 5th, unidentified season. Only the Beasts are involved enough to see these all as connected phenomenon. How far will they go to save their kin? Will they be received as cousins, as saviors or as the hidden source of the afflictions? What will they do when they discover the source lies far inside the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:11:53-07:00","id":945464,"title":"","content":"16) A lone Begotten seeking to expand his Kinship crosses paths with one of the Created. A member of the Osiran Lineage, this Promethean calls himself a Mystic, and seeks to understand humanity through the various supernaturals that dwell among them. It didn't take long for the Beast to find common ground with this intrepid cousin and join him on his Pilgrimage. And so, the journey begins.<br /> <br /> 17) An increasing number of Broods are noticing a rapid shift in the Hive. A raging torrent of superheated winds has begun washing over many of its Chambers, and it has even spilled into sections of a few Lairs. This has been happening since the fiery death of the local Apex. And as they happen with greater frequency and severity, the Children ask themselves the same question. Who or what is now affecting the Hive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T10:10:05-07:00","id":945518,"title":"","content":"18) Some Beasts have started to work more publicly, wearing costumes that reflect their Horrors and fighting crime to feed. That's all fine and dandy, I guess, but now there are a whole bunch of Heroes who've decided to combat them on their level, with massively destructive consequences for human <i>and</i> monstrous bystanders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:05:44-07:00","id":945612,"title":"","content":"19. Rumor has that a rather unusual hero has been putting together teams of beasts to terrorize various local business owners. This hero, whose legend is more of a monster tamer than a monster slayer, is supposedly able to entice these beasts into working for him by using his heroic powers to buff the beasts, which wouldn't be so bad, except the beasts in question act like domesticated pets around him. And worse still, his plots seem to be part of one large master plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:44:04-07:00","id":945841,"title":"","content":"<b>20/)A Mad Mad Mad World:</b> An Eshmaki with a gigantic centipede as a Horror has gone insane, and is gathering Azlu to form a 'hive'. With several Azlu-related Kinship Nightmares, she's cowed the Azlu into absolute obedience. Of course this has drawn increasingly hostile attention from the local Pure. Can the brood solve the issue before the moon-hating werewolves tear the region apart to get at the Azlu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:06:15-07:00","id":946901,"title":"","content":"21: Sheer Bloody Panic<br /> It started out so simply. A report on the 8 o'clock news, some whispers in the downtown neighborhoods and a newspaper add the next morning. The violence in the city is starting on the uptick and the local Beasts couldn't be happier. The widespread media coverage is making the whole town more jumpy, more paranoid and that means feeding is relatively easy. If it had stopped at that point it would have been fine. The panic didn't stop at a few news reports, in fact every day it seems to be getting worse. The Begotten are starting to notice common nightmares among the humans in the area, almost like they're infectious. As the panic virus spreads Dreamers start appearing better armed in their own dreamscape, fending off Beasts that intrude. Humans on the street start becoming more violent. What is the cause of the Panic Virus? Can the Beasts somehow curb it to work for them or will that make it worse? What if it turns out the Beasts are the cause for the spreading Panic, and one of the members of the Brood has become a carrier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:53:01-07:00","id":948171,"title":"","content":"<b>22/) Warbeasts:</b> In a highly rural area, the local Beast hive has exploded into civil war following the death of the old Apex (a Makara); extreme bad blood between both sides greatly hinders ANY attempt at reconciliation... And now, Heroes gather---threatening to doom <i>BOTH</i> Beast factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:07:47-07:00","id":949671,"title":"","content":"<b>23/) King of the Mountain:</b> As the PCs are forced to move to another hive (for whatever reason), they discover an area bereft of all but one Beasts---<i>but</i>, that a <i>huge</i> lurks here, in the Primordial Dream. The area's lone Beast says the Apex (an Ugallu) called a hasty meeting---one the lone Beast couldn't make---and have never reappeared.<br /> <br /> What happened to the hive's population? Does the lone surviving Beast have anything to do with this? And why aren't there <i>any</i> signs of Heroic activity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:04:18-07:00","id":950110,"title":"","content":"Michael Phelps is a Makara Collector. <br /> <br /> Not really a plot hook, just an observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:32:37-07:00","id":950131,"title":"","content":"24) An Incarnate Makara has risen from the depths of the Ocean of Fragments and returned to the world of the living. He calls himself Ammut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:18:49-07:00","id":950656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=950131#post950131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">24) An Incarnate Makara has risen from the depths of the Ocean of Fragments and returned to the world of the living. He calls himself Ammut.</div> </div> </div> </div>24a) The other Ammut would really love to have a talk with him. Expect sudden influxes in mummy related activities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:26:21-07:00","id":951775,"title":"","content":"25) A starving beast hunts trough the local primordial dream. It apparently does not feed at all in the physical world but only in dreams, ignoring the danger of attracting heroeIf the s. If the characters try to track down the beast to stop it, they discover that it is in the local prison. Apparently its homecoming happened while in prison and it lacks the knowledge/chambers to open primordial pathways to free itself. If the characters do nothing it might well die of starvation, but probably not before luring many heroes to town.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:08:52-07:00","id":952267,"title":"","content":"sequel to number 8.<br /> <br /> 26). Just when things started to settle down with your child and your kin's spawn, things get weird again. Someone from the education department has chosen your city to be the location of the first school just for supernatural children and your kin are all enrolling their young in it. However, your mundane child is being let in because the government folks seem to think that they will develop a power that &quot;hasn't been seen in a long time&quot;. What power are these Education department pencil pushers talking about, why did they choose this town to be the location of the campus and what, if anything, does this have to do with the recent cheating and textbook theft scandals in the local schools?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:32:54-07:00","id":952467,"title":"","content":"<b>Their Secret Weapon<br /> <br /> 27)</b> You knew this was coming eventually, there's countless fictional series that feature the same story. The humans that would so arrogantly call themselves &quot;heroes&quot; have finally realized that humans alone may not be enough to win their little war, so they decided to adopt one of us, fresh out of their homecoming and with little experience in supernatural affairs. They've raised her, trained her, and turned her loose upon her kin. Now she is a new kind of predator, one who feeds upon the fears of monsters before striking them down!<br /> <br /> The kin are split on what should be done with her. Some believe it is possible to save this brainwashed sibling, recruiting her into the rest of the family. But others, enraged by such treachery, demand retribution for the murder of their friends and family. While the rest of the family squabbles among themselves, your Brood has decided to take action and seek this hunter out. But the question remains, which side of the argument will you support?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-17-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:01:57-07:00","id":952853,"title":"","content":"28) Some magician has figured out how to bind Horrors to their service, capturing them in stainless steel balls, and now everybody's doing it. What the hell are <i>you</i> gonna do about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:29:02-07:00","id":953126,"title":"","content":"29) At a Crossroads:<br /> You warned her. You all warned her. She was just too young to know any better. It's hard enough to grow up on the street but it must be harder to go through a devouring at 12, to be so bound to the hunger. She couldn't help herself, she'd crawl in through the window at night and steal the other kids toys. Not the whole thing mind you, just the screws, or the batteries. Whatever made it go. There's always a price though, and now you're watching her from the fourth story of a building as the Hero you've all been dodging for months corners her in the alley below. But It didn't go down like you thought, just as you were trying to figure out if you could take the fall you saw him lower his weapon. <br /> <br /> Every time he moved, both you and the girl flinch. The hammer blow never came. He crouched down, gave her some money and brought her into the restaurant around the corner. You kept watching, waiting, expecting the foul play to start. Expecting him to make off with her, to goad her into violence, something. Afterword the girl just said that he was... nice. He's still out there, probably hunting you right now. What will happen if you get the chance to strike first? Can you do it now? Is there really something still human in that thing, and if there is what would you risk to reach it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:33:05-07:00","id":953196,"title":"","content":"<b>Father's Day<br /> <br /> 30)</b> There has been... a noticeable increase to the number of monsters across the world. Where previously only a handful of people would undergo the devouring at a time, that number seems to have almost tripled in recent years. Something out there has been actively spawning the Begotten at an unprecedented rate, and the kin have finally tracked the source back to a single individual. The Begotten are in a frenzy about this news, with many claiming the Dark Mother has returned to her beloved children. But when they finally locate them, they are surprised to find that they are actually male... and they introduce themselves as &quot;Typhon&quot;...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-26-2018, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T12:51:12-07:00","id":953362,"title":"","content":"31. A few months ago you fed on the fear of some Hollywood douche bag who had it coming. Except now, your horror is the dumb monstrous sidekick in a freaking kids show! By the Dark Mother, they sell plush dolls of your horror at toy stores, they even put you in a god damn toothpaste commercial. You need to do something about this before you stop being a source of terror forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-18-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:04:40-07:00","id":953441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=953362#post953362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">31. A few months ago you fed on the fear of some Hollywood douche bag who had it coming. Except now, your horror is the dumb monstrous sidekick in a freaking kids show! By the Dark Mother, they sell plush dolls of your horror at toy stores, they even put you in a god damn toothpaste commercial. You need to do something about this before you stop being a source of terror forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's how we got <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SP-33XI4frs\" target=\"_blank\">Cutethulhu</a><br /> <br /> <b>32)</b> There's a new Brood in the city who seem to feed almost exclusively off criminal elements. One member of the Brood is reported to be quite old, while the others are significantly younger, possibly teenagers who are using their powers to satisfy their adolescent urges. That might not be so bad, except they have recently begun to target their fellow Beasts who are simply looking to feed, under the supposed belief that they are also criminals who should be punished. Those who escape their attacks claim that they were highly skilled in martial combat and there were between 4 and 5 members present at the time. Those with keen senses also note they smelled of the sewers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-18-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:20:33-07:00","id":953617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=953362#post953362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">31. A few months ago you fed on the fear of some Hollywood douche bag who had it coming. Except now, your horror is the dumb monstrous sidekick in a freaking kids show! By the Dark Mother, they sell plush dolls of your horror at toy stores, they even put you in a god damn toothpaste commercial. You need to do something about this before you stop being a source of terror forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, man, the Jersey Devil is a hockey mascot and she gets by fine enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:26:59-07:00","id":953623,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/07/e7/0f/07e70f4d6a3cd9e534d518e0daa159d1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=953617#post953617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, man, 