- even the land itself seems to be affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12513-zaofy","user":"Zaofy","date":". 10-13-2016, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12513-zaofy","name":"Zaofy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:39:43-07:00","id":986839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=953623#post953623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/07/e7/0f/07e70f4d6a3cd9e534d518e0daa159d1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Doesn't really look like how the books describe the two Jersey Devils, does it? This wouldn't effect the real jersey devils.... but the poor Beast in the story hook I gave just got his own cereal, with a cutesy cereal mascot version of him, he's having some issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, he's just gotta own it. He's gotta get into the head of the people making the cartoon, make them make the show subtly scarier and full of unexpected nightmare fuel. I mean, &quot;Five Nights at Freddy's&quot; proves that people can be very scared by unintentionally creepy things. (I'm not saying it's good horror, just that it's successful.<br /> <hr /><b>34)</b> One of your broodmate's cousin's friend's friends say something weird in Silicon Valley. Apparently, somehow, all the AR and VR gadgets are letting normal people see into the Astral, and by extension, see people's Horrors. At first, this was awesome, because you could scare people shitless just by stepping into their peripheral vision, until a Hero realized that it made hunting Beasts and recruiting people to help kill them much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:11:06-07:00","id":986852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=986839#post986839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, he's just gotta own it. He's gotta get into the head of the people making the cartoon, make them make the show subtly scarier and full of unexpected nightmare fuel. I mean, &quot;Five Nights at Freddy's&quot; proves that people can be very scared by unintentionally creepy things. (I'm not saying it's good horror, just that it's successful.<br /> <hr /><b>34)</b> One of your broodmate's cousin's friend's friends say something weird in Silicon Valley. Apparently, somehow, all the AR and VR gadgets are letting normal people see into the Astral, and by extension, see people's Horrors. At first, this was awesome, because you could scare people shitless just by stepping into their peripheral vision, until a Hero realized that it made hunting Beasts and recruiting people to help kill them much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the recent Oculus shit storm regarding the founder's political beliefs was a boon to the beasts in Silicon Valley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:44:50-07:00","id":986867,"title":"","content":"<b>Old Family Recipe<br /> <br /> 35)</b> You've loved grandma's cooking for as long as you can remember, and now she's deemed you worthy to inherit her secret recipes which you may pass onto your own descendants some day. Most of the ingredients are pretty straight forward, except for one item on the list. The primary ingredients in your family's recipes are children (it seems grandma is a Predator), and you're fresh out of stock at the moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Woodland Critters</b><br /> <br /> <b>36) </b>While taking a walk through the forest last night, you met some kin out in the wilds. At least, you think they were kin, because they certainly didn't feel like any natural animals you've ever met. They seemed to be friendly and welcoming enough to you, even offering to accept you into their group. You were even considering visiting them again until you received a letter in the mail the very next morning.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You've been cordially invited to the annual blood orgy this Saturday!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> On the back of the note, you realize are directions leading back through the forest, along with an extra ticket for <i>a guest</i> <i>of your choosing.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T16:02:45-07:00","id":986991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=953623#post953623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/07/e7/0f/07e70f4d6a3cd9e534d518e0daa159d1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Doesn't really look like how the books describe the two Jersey Devils, does it? This wouldn't effect the real jersey devils.... but the poor Beast in the story hook I gave just got his own cereal, with a cutesy cereal mascot version of him, he's having some issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think Frankenberry cereal makes Verney less menacing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:36:57-07:00","id":987309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=986991#post986991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think Frankenberry cereal makes Verney less menacing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, but Prometheans operate off a different set of rules regarding what people think of them. But I agree with Malonkey, turn the show into nightmare fuel.<br /> <br /> 37. The Incarnate apex of the local hive has gone on a trip for a while and has left your brood instructions regarding how their assets are to be managed in their absence. While you are going over their financials, you see a large amount of money being paid to an ordinary mortal every month, but why would the apex be giving that much cash to some seemingly unimportant smuck and can this info help you become the apex before they get back and did the apex want you to find that info?<br /> <br /> 38. A local corporate heiress has some how found out what your brood is and volunteered to be the princess in your lair, organizing your collector's loot and that sort of thing. It seems her rich daddy is trying to force her to marry a self absorbed man that she hates and after learning that her would be finance is an experienced hero, she figured a fake kidnapping by a brood of beasts would be just the way to lure him into a trap and get rid of him.<br /> <br /> Help her, and the brood might just wind up with a wealthy servant who owes them big time but the hero in question is quite dangerous and cunning and she is used to a certain standard of living... is she really worth the trouble?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-14-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:00:38-07:00","id":988268,"title":"","content":"39) Your brood has recently gained a new member, one whose Horror is an Uratha. Not just your average, everyday werewolf, but explicitly one of the half-spirit Forsaken Werewolves. What the Hell is going on here? Did some poor wolf get lost in the Astral and piggyback into somebody's head? Is he just an expression of mythic symbolisms that just happens to line up with the Forsaken?<br /> <br /> 40) You've heard some whispers from an Ogre friend that there's a new escapee in the local Freehold. One who claims he escaped by merging with a monster in a way that's eerily similar to a Devouring. He's clearly not a Begotten, but he's not <i>quite</i> a Changeling, either.<br /> <br /> 41) You've made friends with one of those &quot;Skinchanger&quot; types, what with the magic animal pelt, specifically a lion's pelt. Turns out, &quot;oops,&quot; he was Wolf-blooded, and managed to experience his first Change while in lion form. Your Forsaken friends want you to turn him over, probably either to fix him or kill his ass, but unique Kin like him don't exactly roll along every Tuesday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 10-16-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:23:30-07:00","id":989318,"title":"","content":"42) The last guy your Nemesis fed on was scared out of his mind by whatever you did to him. But he seems to have learned his lesson. But now he's starting to teach other people in the community to stay away from it. Feeding gets a lot more complicated, especially after what he does takes on cult-like forms when others whom you have fed on join in and start to revere your Horror.<br /> It gets worse when they start to get violent and beat up/kill/burn down buildings that you feed on/in and all the commotion starts to draw in heroes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12513-zaofy","name":"Zaofy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:43:18-07:00","id":989797,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">43) <span style=\"color:#000000\">There\u2019s something going on in the Lairs of the Beasts of Chicago. They\u2019re becoming\u2026 regular. Patterned, like a row of cookie-cutter houses in a suburb. Trees in an endless forest become identical, all their branches at the same heights and angles. The storms in a wild ocean blow in at 3:34 every afternoon, precisely. Firestorms swirl in precise Golden Spirals. Even the Horrors are becoming regular and stereotyped. They\u2019re losing identity, individuality.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Can the players uncover the cause of the problem and uproot it, or will the atavistic fear of Chicago\u2019s Dream become banal and trite?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> This is my way of making the Chicago Workings Adventure work for Beast.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-19-2016, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:25:00-07:00","id":991188,"title":"","content":"44) One of your friends, a wizard, has been going nuts about some kind of &quot;door&quot;. He thinks that if it can be charged with the right energies, he can open it to a timeline where Atlantis had never been erased. Eventually, you got him to slow down enough to explain that the last piece he needs is the &quot;essence of Primordial Fear&quot; which sounds right up your alley. He's given you an amulet and told you to feed 'till you're full, but he's been acting real funny. What's <i>really</i> going on here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:59:27-07:00","id":992387,"title":"","content":"An author of Horror stories, who always drew inspiration from his own nightmares. People loved his books: they were somehow more intense, more <i>real </i>than most of the competition.<br /> Then, he was gone, for the better part of a decade. Some said writer's block took another victim, others said he just earned enough and wanted to live out the rest of his life in peace. Some fans claimed the publisher cut him off for one reason or another.<br /> The truth was very different, of course.<br /> When his next book had been published, the fans rejoiced. &quot;Succesfully reinvented himself&quot;, they called it. This was not just because the writing was better than ever. One way or another, he hit a nerve with his new style. Soon enough, even mainstream media took notice of how the visceral disgust he now evoked with his stories was morbidly fascinating. Readers wanted to put the book down, but simply couldn't. Of course, critics laughed at the &quot;horribly stereotypical monster design&quot;. However, when the dark came, they, too, switched on the lights in every room.<br /> Rumour had it that the stories hit some people harder than others; some had outright panic-attacks while reading, some had horrible nightmares for weeks after they finished reading. Those hit the hardest suffered from delusions of <i>something </i>crawling under their skin. It was not long before the first people died, running headlong into traffic, panicking, fleeing a figment of imagination.<br /> The books stopped being produced, but those already out circulated. Youths dared each other to read it. The most prized books were those who were signed.<br /> All critics received signed copies.<br /> Now, one way or another, you got one, too.<br /> <br /> This Namtaru is very strange - and powerful. Which he demonstrates by showing up in the Brood's Lair uninvited, but making it feel like he always belonged to them.<br /> One way or another, he found a way to not just store Nightmares in objects, but to turn the books themselves into an extension of his horror: anywhere his books are, he is, too.<br /> However, whatever he did, it sends out enourmous ripples, attracting heroes to him like bees round a honeypot. Too many for him to deal with, in the long term.<br /> Turning to your group for help, he promises to share his secret with them in exchange for a grisly favour.<br /> <br /> The question is: CAN they help? Will they be able to do what they have to before Chicago is swarmed by Heroes?<br /> And can they trust him? Or should they sacrifice him to save their own hide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  sentence wasn't finished -.- 10-24-2016, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:02:29-07:00","id":992402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=992387#post992387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An author of Horror stories, who always drew inspiration from his own nightmares. People loved his books: they were somehow more intense, more <i>real </i>than most of the competition.<br /> Then, he was gone, for the better part of a decade. Some said writer's block took another victim, others said he just earned enough and wanted to live out the rest of his life in peace. Some fans claimed the publisher cut him off for one reason or another.<br /> The truth was very different, of course.<br /> When his next book had been published, the fans rejoiced. &quot;Succesfully reinvented himself&quot;, they called it. This was not just because the writing was better than ever. One way or another, he hit a nerve with his new style. Soon enough, even mainstream media took notice of how the visceral disgust he now evoked with his stories was morbidly fascinating. Readers wanted to put the book down, but simply couldn't. Of course, critics laughed at the &quot;horribly stereotypical monster design&quot;. However, when the dark came, they, too, switched on the lights in every room.<br /> Rumour had it that the stories hit some people harder than others; some had outright panic-attacks while reading, some had horrible nightmares for weeks after they finished reading. Those hit the hardest suffered from delusions of <i>something </i>crawling under their skin. It was not long before the first people died, running headlong into traffic, panicking, fleeing a figment of imagination.<br /> The books stopped being produced, but those already out circulated. Youths dared each other to read it. The most prized books were those who were signed.<br /> All critics received signed copies.<br /> Now, one way or another, you got one, too.<br /> <br /> This Namtaru is very strange - and powerful. Which he demonstrates by showing up in the Brood's Lair uninvited, but making it feel like he always belonged to them.<br /> One way or another, he found a way to not just store Nightmares in objects, but to turn the books themselves into an extension of his horror: anywhere his books are, he is, too.<br /> However, whatever he did, it sends out enourmous ripples, attracting heroes to him like bees round a honeypot. Too many for him to deal with, in the long term.<br /> Turning to your group for help, he promises to share his secret with them in exchange for a grisly favour.<br /> <br /> The question is: CAN they help? Will they be able to do what they have to before Chicago is swarmed by Heroes?<br /> And can they trust him? Or should they sacrifice him to save their own hide?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it! Sounds absolutely epic, and a fantastic beginning for a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:11:35-07:00","id":992798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=992387#post992387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An author of Horror stories, who always drew inspiration from his own nightmares. People loved his books: they were somehow more intense, more <i>real </i>than most of the competition.<br /> Then, he was gone, for the better part of a decade. Some said writer's block took another victim, others said he just earned enough and wanted to live out the rest of his life in peace. Some fans claimed the publisher cut him off for one reason or another.<br /> The truth was very different, of course.<br /> When his next book had been published, the fans rejoiced. &quot;Succesfully reinvented himself&quot;, they called it. This was not just because the writing was better than ever. One way or another, he hit a nerve with his new style. Soon enough, even mainstream media took notice of how the visceral disgust he now evoked with his stories was morbidly fascinating. Readers wanted to put the book down, but simply couldn't. Of course, critics laughed at the &quot;horribly stereotypical monster design&quot;. However, when the dark came, they, too, switched on the lights in every room.<br /> Rumour had it that the stories hit some people harder than others; some had outright panic-attacks while reading, some had horrible nightmares for weeks after they finished reading. Those hit the hardest suffered from delusions of <i>something </i>crawling under their skin. It was not long before the first people died, running headlong into traffic, panicking, fleeing a figment of imagination.<br /> The books stopped being produced, but those already out circulated. Youths dared each other to read it. The most prized books were those who were signed.<br /> All critics received signed copies.<br /> Now, one way or another, you got one, too.<br /> <br /> This Namtaru is very strange - and powerful. Which he demonstrates by showing up in the Brood's Lair uninvited, but making it feel like he always belonged to them.<br /> One way or another, he found a way to not just store Nightmares in objects, but to turn the books themselves into an extension of his horror: anywhere his books are, he is, too.<br /> However, whatever he did, it sends out enourmous ripples, attracting heroes to him like bees round a honeypot. Too many for him to deal with, in the long term.<br /> Turning to your group for help, he promises to share his secret with them in exchange for a grisly favour.<br /> <br /> The question is: CAN they help? Will they be able to do what they have to before Chicago is swarmed by Heroes?<br /> And can they trust him? Or should they sacrifice him to save their own hide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of In the Mouth of Madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:30:18-07:00","id":992805,"title":"","content":"Is it bad that the first thing I thought of was Garth Marenghi?<br /> <br /> What would his Horror be, space broccoli? A giant wasp? A whisk...to the neck? An angry Scotsman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-25-2016, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:04:58-07:00","id":992903,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\">ajf115</a></b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> thanks^^ Mouth of Madness was actually one of the inspirations for coming up with the character (was meant to be a PC first, but I like it better as a plot hook)!<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> I have to admit I hadn't heard of Garth Marenghi up till now, but that would be another way to go, of course xD<br /> <br /> <br /> There were many construction sites in the City recently, the whole landscape changed. Nobody really paid too much attention to it. However, ever since the new mall And museum Were opened, Something Disturbing has happened: Unchained Register as kin! The Demons feel the god machine's chokehold tightening, while the city ' s Beasts contemplate what family means if it can be toyed with like that. Neither is happy with the new Status quo, and both keep distrusting each other while trying to undo what happened - or do they?<br /> <br /> A beast has fine missing. Since your brood had friendly ties, they Start searching, only to be shocked when finding him. That he is completely catatonic isn't even the worst: he doesnt Register as a beast anymore. There is no familiar Horror, just emptiness. Then, another beast on the same state appears. Feeling more threatened by this than simple death, you Wade through the up-starting rumours to find the culprit, and deal with them Accordingly. Your Main leads: some willworkers are good with souls. Maybe one of them has managed to apply their craft to the Horror, too? Why would he Hunt down Beasts like that?<br /> Alternatively, word has it that there is a new beast in town. They call him Kin-slayer, Devourer. Supposedly, he was a hero who got devoured, or simply really insane. Some say his Horror is different, from so deep that it does not belong to any one family with a very special hunger. Whatever the reason, he Hunt Beasts to devour their horror, leaving an empty Sack of meat behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  No doublepost 10-26-2016, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:25:42-08:00","id":1032199,"title":"","content":"<b>Idea for Fiction Material:</b> A homecoming story involving two best friends who are tragically placed on opposite sides of a war when one of them turns out to be a Beast and the other is a Hero. Just as the young Hero is realizing the truth about monsters, he gets injured in a car accident and his hospitalized. While he's in a coma, his friend begins to realize his own nature and is approaching the time of his transformation. He even comes into contact with a Brood who seem happy to accept him into their fold. While he's coming to grips with the situation, his friend awakens to find they've spontaneously manifested psychic abilities and have begun to heal from their wounds in record time. Perceiving themselves as a super hero, they set out to bring down the monsters of the city, starting with the son of a bitch who hit him with a car!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the driver of said car is none other than a member of his friend's potential new Brood, and during the initial attack, the two friends reunite on bad terms. The young Hero is shocked to find their friend in the company of monsters and even more shocked to hear them trying to stop him from delivering justice! He realizes that his friend is one of them and turns his powers on him in outraged.<br /> <br /> The fight concludes with the accidental death (or perceived death?) of the Hero, despite the young Beast's attempt to save his life. Despondent over being unable to save their childhood companion, the Beast confronts their Horror later that night and accepts their offer to take away their pain. That night, they become a true Beast, joining the very Brood responsible for their friend's descent into madness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Side Note:</b> Although they're pretty sure they watched him fall onto a piece of rebar and get impaled, the Hero's body mysteriously vanishes. They would go on to become a recurring threat in future stories, as their powers continue to refine themselves over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-15-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T13:39:55-07:00","id":1101718,"title":"","content":"<b>48)</b> Something catastrophic struck the city and surrounding areas. No one is sure quite <i>what</i>, but the incident (or the terror it caused) made the whole region into a patchwork of Chambers... and dropped everyone into them. Worse, no one seems to be able to actually leave the Primordial Dream. Now the Hive members find themselves impromptu kings/queens of this new domain - ensuring the survival of their new tenants/prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-09-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:11:50-07:00","id":1101730,"title":"","content":"49 (not counting the fiction hook) ) IRL The Dark Kingdom was a planned Disney park dedicated to the disney villains that was never actually made, but in the CofD, they built it alright and somehow it exists in the physical world and the Primordial Dream at the same time. The Disney corp often hires young begotten from the Florida area to work at the park, the fact that park guest assume their horrors to just be REALLY good costumes and animatronics doesn't change the fact that feeding is easy in the park (and the beasts are paid for doing it).<br /> <br /> Alas, a band of heroes has shown up at the Dark Kingdom and the Disney corp has hired your brood to take care of things before they turn messy and public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T17:43:31-07:00","id":1103338,"title":"","content":"<b>50)</b> It's Mother's Day, and the Brood returns to their communal Lair to find a normal looking, but unnerving and vaguely familiar, woman completely at ease there waiting for them. She claims she is the Dark Mother, and is expecting her present. Is she for real, or is this an elaborate joke? Dare the Brood test her? And what gift could they possibly bring her if they don't?<br /> <br /> <b>51)</b> Halloween is a few weeks away. Powerful members of the local communities of Kin have come to the Brood with an offer: all manner of riches, help against Heroes, and favors in exchange for... acting as hosts and intermediaries for this year's cross-supernatural Monster Mash Ball. [Fill in follow-up plot hooks based on complications as desired]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-13-2017, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T18:52:33-07:00","id":1103354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1103338#post1103338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>50)</b><br /> <b>51)</b> Halloween is a few weeks away. Powerful members of the local communities of Kin have come to the Brood with an offer: all manner of riches, help against Heroes, and favors in exchange for... acting as hosts and intermediaries for this year's cross-supernatural Monster Mash Ball. [Fill in follow-up plot hooks based on complications as desired]</div> </div> </div> </div>51a: The local hunt club is celebrating one of their oldest member's birthday in another part of the same neighborhood, which may or may not be a problem for the Brood attending the monster mash, except the three idiot charmers they sent to pick up the cake are having some bloody hilarious trouble at the bakery...<br /> <br /> 51b: Catering for a bunch of vampires and high Primal urge werewolves will be quite a task...<br /> <br /> 51c: The Brood needs to help some vampires kidnap the DJ for tonight, who couldn't take the gig because he is booked at a nightclub owned by the Russian mafia/The Ashwood Abby.<br /> <br /> 51d: Turns out the reason slutty costumes are so big on Halloween is because of the monster mash, this is THAT kind of party, probably best not to use the ladies of the evening as the catering for the vampires and high urge werewolves.<br /> <br /> 51e: A group of drunk monsters get into a argument about how THEY would have handled the situations in various horror movies about their splats.<br /> <br /> 51f: A young trick r treater dressed as little red riding hood goes through an early first change after showing up at the party house for candy, werewolves get into argument about which pack gets the &quot;cute little puppy&quot;<br /> <br /> 51g: Someone at the party is giving out Arcadian candy (razor blades optional...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T22:43:52-07:00","id":1111560,"title":"","content":"The brood is approached by someone who claims to be the parent/child/spouse/sibling/BFF/whatever of a notorious Hero. This person claims they can &quot;cure&quot; their loved one's &quot;condition&quot; -- they just need Beasts to bait a trap. Is it worth risking your lives on the off chance there really is a way to depower Heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T04:39:21-07:00","id":1135126,"title":"","content":"A Variation on the kinslayer/devourer idea: a Begotten (?) has become megalomaniac. For some reason they Hunt down other Beasts, and seemingly becoming more and more powerful after each they slay. Broodmates Of the slain mention the old chambers being still Inhabited by a now hostile Horror, part of a new Lair. Whatever Atavisms and Lair Traits the slain possessed were now in the murderers Repertoire. The strangest thing? Despite having a large Lair and multiple Horrors, this Killer does not Register as kin. After 3 victims, there was an attempt on a Kin friend of the group - left alive in annoyance because &quot;there's nothing there&quot;. How will the group retaliate? How will they track them down and stopp them?<br /> Think Sylar from Heroes, and you're in the right ballpark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T17:08:55-07:00","id":1151793,"title":"","content":"<b>54)</b> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everyone hail to the pumpkin song</span></b></span></span><br /> A slender, tall, and polite, yet somehow unnerving man has approached the Hive with an offer - he has tired of his throne as the King of Fear, and holding a contest on Halloween night to determine his successor. Whichever Beast can cause the biggest, most inventive scare will win the title. But to make things a bit more interesting, he has:<br /> a) Locked the Beasts into the form of their Horrors - outside their Lair - Halloween night. <br /> b) Decreed that no humans can be harmed by the Beasts. None must die or suffer serious injury due to the Begotten's antics.<br /> c) Cut them off from the powers of their Horrors - Lairs become inaccessible, Nightmares can't be invoked, and Atavisms grant no power - to reduce it down to pure scaring skill.<br /> <br /> Is the brood game? Whoever wins will secure instant elevation to Incarnate and control over a vast Lair with powerful minions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T17:32:57-07:00","id":1151796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1151793#post1151793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>54)</b> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everyone hail to the pumpkin song</span></b></span></span><br /> A slender, tall, and polite, yet somehow unnerving man has approached the Hive with an offer - he has tired of his throne as the King of Fear, and holding a contest on Halloween night to determine his successor. Whichever Beast can cause the biggest, most inventive scare will win the title. But to make things a bit more interesting, he has:<br /> a) Locked the Beasts into the form of their Horrors - outside their Lair - Halloween night.<br /> b) Decreed that no humans can be harmed by the Beasts. None must die or suffer serious injury due to the Begotten's antics.<br /> c) Cut them off from the powers of their Horrors - Lairs become inaccessible, Nightmares can't be invoked, and Atavisms grant no power - to reduce it down to pure scaring skill.<br /> <br /> Is the brood game? Whoever wins will secure instant elevation to Incarnate and control over a vast Lair with powerful minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they're in the shape of monsters, but without any powers? That seems odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T18:11:42-07:00","id":1151803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1151796#post1151796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they're in the shape of monsters, but without any powers? That seems odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adds a handicap. Scaring people is easy when you have the ability to directly inflict fear. Plus it offer scenes where the the scary Beast turns into a bumbling caricature without the powers to back their implied threat.<br /> <br /> Though you could let them have some powers, provided you really enforce the &quot;no harm&quot; constraint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T16:39:04-07:00","id":1152057,"title":"","content":"55. Some heroes who believe in the <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_25101_7-stories-so-horrifying-they-actually-got-cut-from-bible_p2.html\" target=\"_blank\">apocalypse of Baruch</a> think it is the end of the world, and two members of your brood are the monsters humanity is supposed to eat after the torments. Can your brood escape the great monster barbecue?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T17:40:06-07:00","id":1152071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1152057#post1152057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">55. Some heroes who believe in the <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_25101_7-stories-so-horrifying-they-actually-got-cut-from-bible_p2.html\" target=\"_blank\">apocalypse of Baruch</a> think it is the end of the world, and two members of your brood are the monsters humanity is supposed to eat after the torments. Can your brood escape the great monster barbecue?</div> </div> </div> </div>55a. What makes things worse is a group calling itself The Faithful show up with BBQ sauce (and supernatural powers of their own) to help the Heroes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T22:59:29-07:00","id":1152118,"title":"","content":"57: There are rumors among the Children that there is someone wandering the local dreamscape, poking their nose into where it shouldn't be. Problem is, while she's not a Beast, she's using any Nightmares and Atavisms used against her alongside her own substantial bag of tricks, and actually catching her is proving difficult as a result.<br /> <br /> When she's finally pinned down, she explains she's intrigued by what Beasts have at their disposal, and offers her services in exchange for a partnership. Whether she gets declined or not, she terrifies the terrors by unveiling her true form and gives them her name: Miss Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T03:26:00-07:00","id":1152149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1152118#post1152118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">57: There are rumors among the Children that there is someone wandering the local dreamscape, poking their nose into where it shouldn't be. Problem is, while she's not a Beast, she's using any Nightmares and Atavisms used against her alongside her own substantial bag of tricks, and actually catching her is proving difficult as a result.<br /> <br /> When she's finally pinned down, she explains she's intrigued by what Beasts have at their disposal, and offers her services in exchange for a partnership. Whether she gets declined or not, she terrifies the terrors by unveiling her true form and gives them her name: Miss Universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a reference to something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T09:13:29-07:00","id":1152213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1152149#post1152149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a reference to something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly; the idea originates from a character idea of mine, a Demon Integrator who wants to become a new God-Machine effectively, and she believes that doing so requires her to catelogue all supernatural powers...and use them via Show Of Power. Her name Miss Universe is...decidedly literal. Demons also tend to freak Beasts out due to not being a normal supernatural entity, hence the &quot;terrifying the terrors&quot; being.<br /> <br /> However, I didn't explicitely name her as an Unchained because I feel the idea has enough wiggle room for any number of other beings to be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T10:59:05-08:00","id":1159065,"title":"","content":"<b>58) Ahh, Real Monsters:</b> The local Apex has decided to open an academy that caters exclusively to the Begotten somewhere within the Hive. Most of the students are fresh from their devouring and have little experience with what it means to be a literal monster. The academy is here to help provide them with a formal education on such matters and grades them based on their scare tactics, as well as the difficulty of the prey they choose to go after.<br /> <br /> As new Beasts themselves, the players have found themselves inducted into the academy. Unfortunately, they quickly find out that no matter where you go, school is still school...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T11:17:27-08:00","id":1167361,"title":"","content":"(inspired by the CtL 2nd KS)<br /> <br /> 59) The local freehold contacts the brood with a request. One (or more) of their members disappeared through the Gate of Horn, and can't be found anywhere in the Hedge. They suspect the missing changeling may have stumbled into a nightmare thus crossed into the Primordial Dream. They're willing to reward you handsomely if you can find their missing person--perhaps they're a high-ranking member of the Court that's due to come into power soon. But you'll need to find an expert oneiromancer who doesn't want to be found, and persuade them that, out of all the Horrors that roam the Dream, you are the ones they trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:48:59-08:00","id":1193528,"title":"","content":"60) \u200bA Demon somehow becomes the Apex. Normally, this wouldn't be a problem, but this time its wrecking havoc with the entire Hive. Gears smash their way through chambers, Horrors feel on edge, and angels try to invade every single Lair. The Brood needs to either dethrone the Apex, who may not even realize what is happening or find a way to but these extreme effects to an end. Good luck finding the Demon though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-09-2018, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:19:15-08:00","id":1193591,"title":"","content":"61. The most senior Initiate of your Hive calls for a Night of Revels, and your brood takes part in the rite. But the person you see in your vision -- the one who has gravely wronged the Dark Mother and must be ruined utterly -- is a person you know, perhaps a mortal relative or your Kin, who doesn't seem capable of such an offense. Did something go wrong with the rite, or does your loved one have a double life you aren't privy to? Can they possible atone for their crimes against your Mother in a less ruinous way? Should you go along with the demands of the rite -- which is, after all, your Mother's will -- or try to protect your person? <i>Can </i>you protect them, when the entire Hive (and no small number of their Kin) are coming for you?<br /> <br /> 62. When conflict between two broods started to escalate, an elder Beast intervened with a suggestion: instead of fighting each other directly, the broods should each create some Horrorspawn and have them fight each other as proxies, in a contained/controlled environment (such as an unclaimed Chamber). The result is something like a much bloodier version of Pokemon, and long after the original dispute was settled, it's become traditional in the Hive to have these Horrorspawn battles, as much for the entertainment value as to resolve conflict.<br /> <br /> The player brood has just been challenged to such a battle. Horrorspawn, I choose you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T09:42:14-07:00","id":1222672,"title":"","content":"[Awakens from Slumbering in the Lair]<br /> <br /> <b>63)</b> There is a new Apex in the Hive - one of the rare Created. Unfortunately, it is one of the mad Zeky. Worse, the Lair trait they are imposing on the rest if the Hive is <i>Irradiated</i>. Now every time a Primordial Pathway opens, Geiger counters start going off.<br /> <br /> This is drawing entirely too much of the wrong kind of attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:01:39-07:00","id":1222999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1193591#post1193591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">62. When conflict between two broods started to escalate, an elder Beast intervened with a suggestion: instead of fighting each other directly, the broods should each create some Horrorspawn and have them fight each other as proxies, in a contained/controlled environment (such as an unclaimed Chamber). The result is something like a much bloodier version of Pokemon, and long after the original dispute was settled, it's become traditional in the Hive to have these Horrorspawn battles, as much for the entertainment value as to resolve conflict.<br /> <br /> The player brood has just been challenged to such a battle. Horrorspawn, I choose you!</div> </div> </div> </div><b>64)</b> The God-Machine has begun an assault on the Beasts of the local Hive. But rather than clever traps, or powerful Angels, it is sending waves of suicide-bombing Imperatives against the targeted Beast's Lair. They try not to engage and just rush their way to the Heart Chamber, then start to collapse it. The Begotten have responded by creating a maze of defenses to destroy the intruders (without baring their passage enough to get them to just collapse the current Chamber). Your Brood is now playing Tower Defense in their soul for keeps - at least until the source can be destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T17:23:21-07:00","id":1223068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=986867#post986867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Old Family Recipe<br /> <br /> 35)</b> You've loved grandma's cooking for as long as you can remember, and now she's deemed you worthy to inherit her secret recipes which you may pass onto your own descendants some day. Most of the ingredients are pretty straight forward, except for one item on the list. The primary ingredients in your family's recipes are children (it seems grandma is a Predator), and you're fresh out of stock at the moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Woodland Critters</b><br /> <br /> <b>36) </b>While taking a walk through the forest last night, you met some kin out in the wilds. At least, you think they were kin, because they certainly didn't feel like any natural animals you've ever met. They seemed to be friendly and welcoming enough to you, even offering to accept you into their group. You were even considering visiting them again until you received a letter in the mail the very next morning.<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;You've been cordially invited to the annual blood orgy this Saturday!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> On the back of the note, you realize are directions leading back through the forest, along with an extra ticket for <i>a guest</i> <i>of your choosing.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yah blood orgy ,!!!!,I\u2019m gussing one is pregnant and being stalked be a mountain lion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T10:10:50-07:00","id":1233455,"title":"","content":"65) A throng of prometheans have moved into your territory, believing one of their members will reach the new dawn. With them is a familiar inguma that you remember having left for a chance at a long lasting kinship. While all seems well since the throng won't be in town long, a promethean asks for help, saying their beast friend seems to be holding back their ascending throng member. Will you convince the inguma he needs to let go, or let him convince you it's best for the promethean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T07:40:19-07:00","id":1236402,"title":"","content":"Becoming a Beast does not mean one loses their patriotitism. <br /> A Brood of foreign soldiers Starts a sort- of invasion when hard tolls are levied upon their country, sekeing to lay waste to the players' City due to its financial, military or economic importance in retribution. And feed their Hungers for Ruin and Punishment by doing so. Before they get to work, however, they make sure to fill up to the top, so they can absolutely Thresh the place.<br /> <br /> As they are aware how much damage even a single gorged Begotten can wreak, the Brood has to act, and fast. How will they find them, and how might they stop them?<br /> <br /> It would make sense to give the invaders large - scale atavisms Like storm-lashed, titanic blow, Plague Bearer etc. Nightmares like The Water Wont Last and Your Rage Consumes You in combination with Fear is contagious also would be useful. Environment 4 Lair Traits would also help a lot.<br /> Keep in mind that the destruction of the city, which is the invaders' goal, will automatically draw every supernatural inhabitant's ire-they should have corresponding power/connections. The players should use that to their advantage nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:45:05-07:00","id":1236497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1236402#post1236402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a Beast does not mean one loses their patriotitism.<br /> <b>66)</b> A Brood of foreign soldiers Starts a sort- of invasion when hard tolls are levied upon their country, sekeing to lay waste to the players' City due to its financial, military or economic importance in retribution. And feed their Hungers for Ruin and Punishment by doing so. Before they get to work, however, they make sure to fill up to the top, so they can absolutely Thresh the place.<br /> <br /> As they are aware how much damage even a single gorged Begotten can wreak, the Brood has to act, and fast. How will they find them, and how might they stop them?<br /> <br /> It would make sense to give the invaders large - scale atavisms Like storm-lashed, titanic blow, Plague Bearer etc. Nightmares like The Water Wont Last and Your Rage Consumes You in combination with Fear is contagious also would be useful. Environment 4 Lair Traits would also help a lot.<br /> Keep in mind that the destruction of the city, which is the invaders' goal, will automatically draw every supernatural inhabitant's ire-they should have corresponding power/connections. The players should use that to their advantage nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>67)</b> The assault of the Invading Brood has left scars, but was repelled before it could cause irreparable damage. However, it seems to have broken something stranger - the local dreamscape is now being invaded by legions of Dreamborn, some of them even entering the material world and causing havoc. Your Kin are in damage control mode, so it falls to you and your Brood to repel these <i>other</i> aggressors and resolve whatever triggered this invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-20-2018, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:10:31-07:00","id":1236527,"title":"","content":"68)<br /> One of your chambers' physical locations was somehow swallowed by the underworld.<br /> You have a chamber there now, which Grants you access to many a nifty thing. It has become a great base for your power. The Broods Makara especially Loves the Waters there and claims to have met 'the big brother'.<br /> However, soon you are under constant Assault of strange dead and even never living things for having broken some &quot;Old Law&quot;.<br /> Worse, the Waters are changing your Aquatic sibling, Forcing a pseudo-merging into a Rampant Beast as his Personality wanes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T05:10:05-07:00","id":1252487,"title":"","content":"One plot I am running currently:<br /> 69)<br /> Two of the Begotten have become a couple and are now expecting a child! To celebrate, the local Initiate offers to hold a ceremony of blessing for the child, in which the soon-to-be parents receive a vision of their future child.<br /> However, instead of a normal human being, or a Begotten, they see their child becoming an Insatiable!<br /> To avert this fate, they need to travel deep into the Dark Mother's Lands, and from there pass through layers and layers of the Primordial, to hasten the gestating Horror Larvae's development and make sure it turns out to be a normal Horror, or something resembling it, when the time comes.<br /> Will that work? And what effects will passing through the Dark Mother's Lands have on an unborn being?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T09:48:21-07:00","id":1252531,"title":"","content":"<b>70)</b> You feel something happen to one of your Chambers, but when you investigate, nothing seems out of place.<br /> A few nights later, when your Horror goes hunting through your Lair, it encounters one of your Kin... except they aren't Kin, but human. You check on them afterwards, and yep - they still aren't human.<br /> When you open a Primordial Pathway from the Chamber, you emerge into a different Earth, one where your Kin never became such, among other differences. This only happens when you exit via that Chamber.<br /> <br /> <b>71)</b> (follow up, though not strictly necessary, of 70)<br /> One night when entering your Lair, you meet a mysterious man in an anachronistic suit. He wants to contract with you into using your Chambers as a medium for travel to and connecting to alternative realities. And, should you find the venture favorable, act as spokesman to others of your kind so as to expand the offerings available.<br /> He seems like Kin, though none you've ever encountered before. He's vague when talking about how he can manage this, though he states that is more due to lacking the words to communicate it properly than secretive intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-08-2018, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:25:00-08:00","id":1357874,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m taking inspiration for this Plot-Hook from the Horrorspawn idea proposed by Mad-Maudlin.<br /> <br /> <b>72)</b> A local brood of surprisingly imaginative Beasts have founded a tournament around the region's Horrorspawn fights entitled as \u2018The Terror Games!\u2019 The seven of them are offering an unknown \u2018Ultimate Prize\u2019 to any who can both win the tournament and best them. Not only that, but, if the news on the supernatural grapevine is to be believed, the Brood has somehow managed to link the position of Apex and the tournament\u2019s championship title \u2018Lord/Lady of Fear\u2019 together. The Brood has a chance to sign up, but only one of the Begotten is able to win the chanpionship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1151803#post1151803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adds a handicap. Scaring people is easy when you have the ability to directly inflict fear. Plus it offer scenes where the the scary Beast turns into a bumbling caricature without the powers to back their implied threat.<br /> <br /> Though you could let them have some powers, provided you really enforce the &amp;quot;no harm&amp;quot; constraint.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s also a possible in-universe reason why the Brood can\u2019t access their Atavisms. Such things are essentially the Begotten channelling a portion of their true visages into their human forms. Ergo, they can\u2019t channel such into their bodies since they\u2019re already <i>in</i> their true forms.<br /> <br /> Edit: Decided to change up my plot hook slightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 01-17-2020, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T02:08:59-08:00","id":1359228,"title":"","content":"73) <br /> Begotten and Unchained don't work together, usually. They do have much to give to each other, however, and occasionally, strike up a partnership.<br /> One such pair has been working for decades. The Ugallu tyrant has been Mayor and Apex for almost two decades now, and with his unlikely partner, they've completely redesigned the place. They were intent on changing the Infrastructure, and acquiring and integrating key Chambers as well as Obcasus Rites through prodigious use. Now, they have almost reached their goal and enlist the Brood to help them to reap their ultimate rewards: the entrance to the Primordial Dream is to be ripped open, turning the whole area into a gateway to the Mother's Land. All they need to do is performing human sacrifices of powerful people in different places over a short period. The leaders remind them that the rewards would be immense, but should they not agree, they'd find someone else. A pack of Pure, a Kindred Coterie, another Brood - the list of possible help is long enough. <br /> But will this truly achieve the leader's dreams of rising up to Incarnate and creating their own Hell, save from the G-M for good? How will the inhabitants (both mundane and supernatural) react to living in a Nightmare version of their city, with some among them suddenly appearing to be horrific monsters? How will the rest of the world react when they learn of this abrupt change? <br /> How will the Dark Mother react? Can the Brood stop this madness - do they even want to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T17:19:05-08:00","id":1368176,"title":"","content":"Inspired by a comment made over on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863020-inspirational-images-for-beast?p=1181707#post1181707\">Inspirational Images For Beast Thread</a>.<br /> <br /> 74) A local Beast (an Ugallu who's Horror bears a striking resemblance to <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kgoggles/art/Encounters-with-the-Imaginary-Simurgh-626727713\" target=\"_blank\">the Simurgh</a>, to be exact) has recently revealed that She's been raising a child (or group of children) inside her Lair. She now approaches the PC Brood in a state of near panic and extreme worry; (one or more of) her child(ren) ha(s/ve) been kidnapped and are being held hostage by a Hero convinced that they know her \u2018weakness\u2019. She wants aid in the rescuing of her little one(s). Will the Troupe answer the call? And how has living inside a Lair for pretty much their entire li(fe/ves) affected the child(ren)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 03-23-2025, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T10:02:28-08:00","id":1371993,"title":"","content":"Came up with the first idea after watching Bambi 2 and doing a bit of thinking on it, during which my thoughts somehow went into B:tP territory.<br /> <br /> 75) <u><b>Terror-Fawn!</b></u> While out on a Summer-long group Hike through a particularly large forest/wood, the players come upon something absolutely shocking; a young fawn (or some other woodland critter) who registers as Kin! To be more specific, the little one\u2019s a Beast! What does the Brood do with this apparent anomaly? How will the rest of the Begotten react to this discovery?? What does it mean if \u2018mere\u2019 animals can become Devoured by Horrors??? <i>And just HOW did this even happen in the first place????</i><br /> <br /> 76) <u><b>The Kindgdom of Horror</b></u>; A Brood has just gone \u2018Dark Lord\u2019 and conquered a small country. They\u2019ve started to invite both fellow Begotten and various Kin along to become citizens in this new \u2018Kingdom of Horror\u2019.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvedulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=924713#post924713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>10) The Corrupting Touch</b></u><br /> <br /> Something strange is happening to the local area's Begotten, or more precisely, to the targets of their feeding. Some people who are fed on by Beasts are changing, their bodies warping to reflect the Horror of the Beast that fed on them. A Namtaru whose Horror manifests as a massive horned rat might cause their greasy black or brown body hair to grow over their victim's bodies, faces becoming elongated and muscles twitchy. An Anakim whose Horror takes the form of a shambling mass of blood-soaked metal shards finds that his last meal has gone into hiding as weird metallic growths manifest under the skin.<br /> <br /> Making a bad situation worse, those who are warped by a Beast's Horror gain the ability to sense the presence of the Begotten, with a particularly strong connection to the monster with whom their condition originates. Beasts in your city are now gaining collections of weird hangers-on. Obsessed cultists, children trying to please their cruel creator gods, hating and loving the Begotten all at once. What will you do when even your gentle feedings may leave scars?</div> </div> </div> </div>77) A new religion has recently sprung up. Usually this wouldn\u2019t mean anything to the local Begotten, until a week ago, when a Beast investigating the whole shebang came back reporting something that no-one expected; this Religion worships the Dark Mother Herself, glorifying her offspring as Demigods! What do the players do with this new information?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=952853#post952853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">28) Some magician has figured out how to bind Horrors to their service, capturing them in stainless steel balls, and now everybody's doing it. What the hell are <i>you</i> gonna do about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>28-A) A couple of these so called \u2018trainers\u2019 have started performing knock-off Pokem\u00f3n-Style fights with their captured Horrors, competing over bragging rights and bets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1159065#post1159065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>58) Ahh, Real Monsters:</b> The local Apex has decided to open an academy that caters exclusively to the Begotten somewhere within the Hive. Most of the students are fresh from their devouring and have little experience with what it means to be a literal monster. The academy is here to help provide them with a formal education on such matters and grades them based on their scare tactics, as well as the difficulty of the prey they choose to go after.<br /> <br /> As new Beasts themselves, the players have found themselves inducted into the academy. Unfortunately, they quickly find out that no matter where you go, school is still school...</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of Monsters University. Was that part of your inspiration?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvedulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=924246#post924246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>7) You Meddling Kids!</b></u><br /> The aftermath of some of your more... <i>creative</i> feedings has always drawn people - gawkers ready to build your legend or baffled cops, the occassional wild-eyed Hero. Now, however, your trail has been picked up by a group of amateur monster hunters. You'd classify these annoyingly persistent sleuths as Heroes except for two things. First, they haven't tried to kill you, and second, they are totally convinced that you are a <i>fake</i>. Even repeated use of Nightmares hasn't seemed to deter the investigators. Even if they're not actively malevolent, their prying might lead a Hero to you or to your Family in the city's supernatural underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, <i><b>BOY</b></i>, those kids\u2019re gonna need a fresh set of underwear when they realise that the Beast is for real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 04-19-2020, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T11:44:33-08:00","id":1373412,"title":"","content":"<b><u>78) Federal Begotten of Investigation</u></b>: The moment Agent Langston saw you, you saw him - and the Stalker in Streets mirrored the exact look of disgust as his human body did. Langston's first experience with the supernatural was before his Devouring, you see; he was one of the Vanguard Serial Crime Unit's top profilers due to his ability to understand slashers intuitively even without their pet psionic projects. When VASCU was forced to go private, he stayed with the Feds, where away from his ability to constantly focus on looking outward at the dark things he hunted, he turned inward towards his dreams, where the Stalker finally caught up to his soul and revealed his natural talent was due to having more in common with the supernatural murderers than his fellow agents. He's never quite forgiven himself for it, and while he's channeled it into a very productive end of at least attempting to rehabilitate slashers (and taking what food he can when it's a lost cause), he's absolutely certain he, and anyone like him, is a form of psychic Undertaking - and given how he saw you around an actual murdered corpse, his mind has leapt to the worst possible conclusion. You have a wayward brother who started off with a lot more experience in running people down after you than you did when you were Devoured, and he's kept in touch with his friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-08-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T09:17:01-07:00","id":1373770,"title":"","content":"Was going through the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks/page5\">H:TV Story Hook Thread</a>, when, upon reading a very particular <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=199188#post199188\">couple</a> of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/153488-1001-hunter-story-hooks?p=199197#post199197\">posts</a> and letting them stew in my mental cauldron for a few minutes, my mind vomited forth the following Plot Hook Idea!<br /> <br /> 79) One of the PCs learns that their Boyfriend/Girlfriend/Lover/Fiancee/Husband/Wife/Romantic Significant Other* is a Noble, and vice versa (albeit for the Brood as a whole^). How does the PC and Brood deal with this revelation and discovery?<br /> <br /> *Delete as appropriate.<br /> ^If applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T12:49:05-07:00","id":1373803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1371993#post1371993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 28-A) A couple of these so called \u2018trainers\u2019 have started performing knock-off Pokem\u00f3n-Style fights with their captured Horrors, competing over bragging rights and bets.</div> </div> </div> </div>doing that with spirits and goetia is so much simpler/safer that I really can't see that happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T14:11:11-07:00","id":1373991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1373803#post1373803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">doing that with spirits and goetia is so much simpler/safer that I really can't see that happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>No-one said such people had to be 'sane', 'smart', 'intelligent' and/or 'sensible' in any capacity we recognise and/or understand as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 03-17-2020, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:01:55-07:00","id":1379839,"title":"","content":"77) You've recently encountered a Begotten-made Promethean. It's pretty interesting.<br /> It's obsessed with teaching lessons, well past the point that Begotten are. That's not the problem. The lessons are good. Great even. Some might even say that this creature is better at teaching lessons than Begotten are.<br /> The problem is the Wasteland, causing people to automatically fall into the Primordial Dream whenever they go to sleep.<br /> The other problem is the Disquiet, slowly infecting the masses with unthinking fear.<br /> How are you going to solve this problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:04:36-07:00","id":1379840,"title":"","content":"78) The Primordial Dream experiences something that is being called a &quot;dreamquake&quot;. The bonds between Chambers in Lairs become damaged, among other things.<br /> While people are cleaning up from this unexpected event, you are approached by a Begotten from a Family you don't recognize &amp; have never heard of before.<br /> And then, it comes out that something momentous happened before the dreamquake. An Unchained managed to make contact with the the Dark Mother &amp; beseeched her for a safe place &amp; to be part of the family. The Dark Mother decided to show kindness on this kinda pathetic creature (because it was).<br /> That moment caused the dreamquake, created the Automata Family.<br /> Now everyone is asking has this happened before? How does this effect our relations with Unchained as a whole? What are the capabilities of the Automata Family? Where do we go from here?<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Unchained still do not register as kin, that is unchanged. This is no different even if you are part of the Automata Family.<br /> \u2022 The dreamquake happened because Unchained have no kinship with Begotten, &amp; the Dark Mother had to do something extra to make this work.<br /> \u2022 The Automata Family have Birthrights, Atavisms, &amp; stuff connected to espionage, demonism, &amp; technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:07:21-07:00","id":1379841,"title":"","content":"79) You're exploring the Primordial Dream in the area where your Lair is one day when you come across a single Chamber, all by its lonesome, occupied by a single human.<br /> You ask around about this &amp; learn that while this is a rare phenomena, it has happened before. Some people just manifest a single Chamber in the Primordial Dream. This will never grow beyond one Chamber.<br /> None of this is the problem. The problem is that you know the human in question from your human life, &amp; they recognized you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:08:06-07:00","id":1379842,"title":"","content":"80) Begotten in the area are unpredictably going through randomized Inheritances. There is nothing in the way of rhyme or reason to this. What will happen when it becomes your turn, or will something stop it before it gets to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:08:51-07:00","id":1379845,"title":"","content":"81) The Apex is Dead. Long Live the Apex.<br /> And from the corpse of the late Apex is leaking some weird energy causing anyone close enough to warp into a new variety of Begotten-Spawn.<br /> How will you react to all these brand new &quot;little cousins&quot; appearing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:10:14-07:00","id":1379846,"title":"","content":"82) There's a Nightmare Maelstrom ripping through the region, getting towards the end, but it would be a very bad thing if it got all the way through the cycle.<br /> You identify a stream of energy in the air. It's some sort of aura leakage coming off of the person at the centre of the Maelstrom.<br /> You follow the stream &amp; find... an old, close friend from high school who you feel out of touch with. This is something of a complication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:11:54-07:00","id":1379847,"title":"","content":"83) You've just gone through your Devouring, &amp; your Horror is a creature ripped straight out of the Supernal Realms.<br /> Normally you might be asking how, but creatures of the Supernal Realms can only last so long outside of the Supernal Realms before they keel over dead.<br /> The clock is ticking...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:12:33-07:00","id":1379850,"title":"","content":"84) New Begotten are popping out of the woodwork. However, whereas normal Begotten feed on fear these ones feed on regret, hope, rage, love, sloth, faith, greed, gluttony, etc.<br /> Where are these weird Begotten coming from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:14:05-07:00","id":1379851,"title":"","content":"85) Your brood has been approached by an Insatiable who has an unusual request. They have come to the conclusion that the process that makes an Insatiable is effectively a broken Devouring. They want you to fix them. They want you to turn them from an Insatiable into a Begotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:33:05-07:00","id":1380274,"title":"","content":"86) The Dark Mother looked at her children, the Geryo, &amp; reminisced of the long-dead Power called Urfarah.<br /> Then she decided to decided to have a new mass of children, but not ones like the Begotten. She's thinking of babies more on the level of Geryo, &amp; for such spawn, she will need a suitable mate.<br /> To find one she's decided to poke a metaphorical wasps nest with a stick &amp; see what comes out. Lucky you, you live in the selected, metaphorical wasps nest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:35:47-07:00","id":1380276,"title":"","content":"87) Well, that happened. The Dark Mother has mated &amp; is now carrying a large number of baby monsters. She's approaching giving birth. One of the babies is going to be dropped down in the city where you live.<br /> You have no idea what you're in for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:39:06-07:00","id":1380278,"title":"","content":"88)Impossibly enough, an Insatiable has becme the local Apex...and now, every Lair in the Hive begins developing Lair Traits---MULTIPLE Lair Traits that NOONE is immune to'! The Primordial Dream quakes under the mystic strain of this arcane cancer, and it's up to the players' brood to put things right!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T22:59:43-07:00","id":1380322,"title":"","content":"89) The Primordial Dream is mysteriously wrapping itself around a young woman, barely legal. Investigation reveals that she's pregnant &amp; that the sperm involved was perfectly normal sperm, the egg appears to show evidence that it comes from the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> How the characters uncover this information is up is completely up in the air fair as I'm convinced, that part just doesn't feel like it matters as much in the long term. The plot hook is basically my attempt at the Dark Mother &quot;recreating&quot; the virgin birth from the Bible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:53:55-07:00","id":1380400,"title":"","content":"90)Not every Beast is s friend of the extended family. Such is the case of Manny &quot;the Iron Bull&quot; Danswool, a Minotaur-Horror Talassi who works as a makeshift Huntsman for various Gentry. Unfazed by the normal rules Huntsmen must abide by, Manny has become the scourge of freehold a throughout the area.<br /> <br /> Changeling Kin approach the players' characters, begging for help.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, one of Manny's Chambers is in the Hedge---while another Chamber is <i>in Arcadia itself</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:27:32-07:00","id":1380429,"title":"","content":"91)A Namtaru with an ichneuman-Horror has developed a grotesque Birthright enabling her to &quot;implant&quot; back-up copies of herself in mortals. Should she die, her body crumbles to ash, and the nearest such host explodes in a spectacular shower of gore, revealing the Namtaru, resurrected and healthy once more!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, every time she resurrects, she gains a new Hero obsessed with killing her. Nearly a decade after her Devouring, this Namtaru now has a band of eleven allied Heroes hunting her down,<br /> <br /> Now she's in the brood's territory, dragging these Heroes in her wake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:13:07-07:00","id":1380688,"title":"","content":"92)In the city of [Fill-In-The-Blank], a revolution has occurred, leading to the worst supernatural elements seizing control,<br /> <br /> You see, an Insatiable and its allies---a war host of Pure werewolves---has seized power, supernaturally speaking, over [Fill-In-Tje-Blank], and things are beginning to deteriorate rather badly. Spirits are crossing the Gauntlet in ever-growing numbers, and the Pure are helping the Insatiable hunt down the city's remaining Beasts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:32:48-07:00","id":1381013,"title":"","content":"93)Two Beasts engage in a &quot;Hatfields and McCoys&quot; type of blood feud, which spirals out of control. Heroes start to appear in ever-greater numbers. Can the brood negotiate a peace, or will this blood feud reach its seemingly inevitable conclusion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T13:23:14-07:00","id":1381970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1381013#post1381013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">93)Two Beasts engage in a &amp;quot;Hatfields and McCoys&amp;quot; type of blood feud, which spirals out of control. Heroes start to appear in ever-greater numbers. Can the brood negotiate a peace, or will this blood feud reach its seemingly inevitable conclusion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya\u2019 know\u2026 with a little bit of modification on either end (depending on ST discretion), this could be used as a lead in to Story Hooks 62 and 72 (created by Mad_Maudlin and I respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T17:56:10-07:00","id":1382021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1381970#post1381970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ya\u2019 know\u2026 with a little bit of modification on either end (depending on ST discretion), this could be used as a lead in to Story Hooks 62 and 72 (created by Mad_Maudlin and I respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally see that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T04:52:58-07:00","id":1382122,"title":"","content":"94) A Geryo has injected itself inside the Primordial Dream of a domain, quickly becoming the Apex due to its sheer power.<br /> It spreads itself through the Dream, spreading like some disturbing, cancerous growth, adding Chambers &amp; Lairs to its vast body. Any Begotten that gets too close risks becoming infected by the &quot;Distortion&quot;, which is getting harder every day.<br /> The growth cannot be hurt at just random point. Only at its central mass can the monster be felled. But at that point, the risk of Distortion infection is guaranteed.<br /> Options are sparse. In fact, there appears to be only one. We need a Hero, or possibly a team of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T17:33:19-07:00","id":1382270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1382021#post1382021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally see that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>know</i>, right?! And it could be used for inter-Chronicle references! The PC Brood manages to diplomance, intimidate, trick or otherwise 'persuade' the two Elder Beasts (or Broods, or it could have already happened) into performing the fight, which then spirals into a regional tradition before yet another group of Begotten create a tournament out of it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:49:15-07:00","id":1384330,"title":"","content":"95) You get attacked by a Beast Rampant but manage to beat the creature back, forcing it to retreat &amp; lick its wounds.<br /> Your brood follows it to find it encounter a willworker, &amp; be treated gently. The willworker cleans its wounds, telling it a story in the process.<br /> When you confront the willworker, they claim that the Beast is their brother/sister/sibling, &amp; that they intend to reverse the Merger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:39:04-07:00","id":1386191,"title":"","content":"96) You find a legendary Begotten with a reputation for killing Begotten that have &quot;gone astray&quot; waiting for you in your Lair.<br /> Good news, they're not here for you. They need your help in getting to their current target, the local Apex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:39:59-07:00","id":1386192,"title":"","content":"97) Fallout from some recent incident (feel free to decide what the incident was) has resulted in who the Apex is, changing on a daily basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:41:11-07:00","id":1386193,"title":"","content":"98) You're a newly Devoured Begotten &amp; have just been told of the terrifying, tyrannical local Apex.<br /> Meanwhile, the Devouring has given you a confidence boost. You're gonna strike up a conversation with your crush, get to know them better, maybe ask them out on a date?<br /> Wait, what's that power seeping off of your crush? Oh crap, your crush is the local Apex.<br /> \u25cf I've left this vague enough so that you can decide whether the Apex is tyrant ruler or a fairly decent ruler. Whether the accusations are built off of baseless dislike of their rule, a grab for power, or something concrete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:11:00-07:00","id":1386591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1386193#post1386193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">98) You're a newly Devoured Begotten &amp; have just been told of the terrifying, tyrannical local Apex.<br /> Meanwhile, the Devouring has given you a confidence boost. You're gonna strike up a conversation with your crush, get to know them better, maybe ask them out on a date?<br /> Wait, what's that power seeping off of your crush? Oh crap, your crush is the local Apex.<br /> \u25cf I've left this vague enough so that you can decide whether the Apex is tyrant ruler or a fairly decent ruler. Whether the accusations are built off of baseless dislike of their rule, a grab for power, or something concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>For added hilarity, the Apex could be a particularly Cute, Adorable, Adorably Cute, Cutely Adorable, nigh-impossibly Sweet Cinnamon Roll of a freshly Blossomed <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/home\" target=\"_blank\">Noble</a> ((S)He having Blossomed around the same time the previous Apex lost the Position and accidentally took it for him/herself) with the Small-Framed and Onceborn Merits. The sheer WTF?!ing of the players would be DELICIOUS!! Especially if they wound up taking the Apex Noble into their Brood without realising his/her position in the hive. And even <b><i>MORE</i></b> so is the Noble was a PC and neither the character or the player <i>knew of their postion in the <b>first place!</b></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1386191#post1386191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">96) You find a legendary Begotten with a reputation for killing Begotten that have &quot;gone astray&quot; waiting for you in your Lair.<br /> Good news, they're not here for you. They need your help in getting to their current target, the local Apex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! The bowl-loosening effect of finding such a Sibling in their (shared(?)) Lair would be an awesome, hilarious, hilariously awesome and awesomely hilarious brown note moment for the players!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 05-07-2020, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:44:57-07:00","id":1387226,"title":"","content":"99) The Dark Mother has declared war upon the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:45:32-07:00","id":1387227,"title":"","content":"100) The Dark Mother has requested that you eliminate one of your &quot;siblings&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:46:28-07:00","id":1387228,"title":"","content":"101) Your here it echoing through the Primordial Dream, back &amp; forth, back &amp; forth. The Dark Mother is getting back together with her husband, the Primogenitor. And she wants his children &amp; hers to get along.<br /> \u25cf This doesn't have to be accurate, maybe it's some sort free-floating Nightmare risen from the dreams of a Begotten. Maybe there's another explanation. Get creative with possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:24:35-07:00","id":1387245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1386591#post1386591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For added hilarity, the Apex could be a particularly Cute, Adorable, Adorably Cute, Cutely Adorable, nigh-impossibly Sweet Cinnamon Roll of a freshly Blossomed <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/home&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Noble</a> ((S)He having Blossomed around the same time the previous Apex lost the Position and accidentally took it for him/herself) with the Small-Framed and Onceborn Merits. The sheer WTF?!ing of the players would be DELICIOUS!! Especially if they wound up taking the Apex Noble into their Brood without realising his/her position in the hive. And even <b><i>MORE</i></b> so is the Noble was a PC and neither the character or the player <i>knew of their postion in the <b>first place!</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I am of two minds of this idea.<br /> On the one hand, I have trouble seeing a Noble, especially a freshly Blossomed one, as the Apex.<br /> On the other hand, I can totally see a Noble keeping hold of the position once they learn about it, just so they can use the authority it gives them to try &amp; make some Begotten generally be decent people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:16:02-07:00","id":1387366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1387245#post1387245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am of two minds of this idea.<br /> On the one hand, I have trouble seeing a Noble, especially a freshly Blossomed one, as the Apex.<br /> On the other hand, I can totally see a Noble keeping hold of the position once they learn about it, just so they can use the authority it gives them to try &amp; make some Begotten generally be decent people.</div> </div> </div> </div>In response to your two minds;<br /> <br /> 1) Part of the lure would be finding/figuring out just how, exactly, the Noble actually became the Apex instead of someone else. Like, say, another Beast, a Mage, a Changeling, a Sin-Eater, one of the Arisen, or otherwise.<br /> <br /> 2) They\u2019d also be highly dubious about whether or not to keep their position upon learning about how it is earned, since a good portion of the local populace would need to be scared of them enough for the Noble to appear in their nightmares. Ergo, the Prince(ss) would have to be feared to try doing some good... which might actually help them understand the Begotten\u2019s side of things, at least a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 05-10-2020, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:46:08-07:00","id":1387593,"title":"","content":"Hey Kratos, please keep em in one post if you can. Friendly reminder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a