7593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Kratos, please keep em in one post if you can. Friendly reminder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean keep each plot hook in its own post, or put all the plot hooks I'm currently posting in one post simultaneously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T17:57:06-07:00","id":1387622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1387620#post1387620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean keep each plot hook in its own post, or put all the plot hooks I'm currently posting in one post simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try to collect your entries into one big post.<br /> <br /> 1:]<br /> 2:]<br /> 3:]<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> It's not a huge deal but a preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T20:07:22-07:00","id":1387634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874976-1001-beast-story-hooks?p=1387622#post1387622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try to collect your entries into one big post.<br /> <br /> 1:]<br /> 2:]<br /> 3:]<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> It's not a huge deal but a preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the clarification. I will try to keep to it in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:31:40-07:00","id":1391442,"title":"","content":"102) Any Heroes in the area have started getting attacked by people from a group called the Reckoning.<br /> That in itself would be fine, the average Hero is something of a shithead in your opinion, but these people don't draw any lines between &quot;good&quot; Heroes &amp; &quot;bad&quot; Heroes.<br /> Your sister is a good Hero, you have a very positive relationship with her that only grew stronger upon the two of you leaving humanity behind. Your sister just became the Reckoning's newest target.<br /> \u25cf Uses the Reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T00:10:26-08:00","id":1425323,"title":"","content":"103) A Begotten appears, claiming to possess an Obcasus Rite that allows Begotten to turn Anathema back on the Heroes that impose them. What they don't say is how the energies of the rite result in eventualities far worse than dealing with a simple Anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:15:09-08:00","id":1438386,"title":"","content":"104) Ancient stories of a truly Mighty Incarnate Beast*, their powerful Hero Arch-Nemesis* the enmity between them and the final duel that resulted in the both of them seemingly dying, have circulated throughout the region for close on a millennium. Now, however, signs have started to crop up, hinting that the Incarnate isn't quite dead (and maybe never has been). Eventually, Members of the Incarnate's Begotten following approach the Brood, asking for aid in ensuring their 'Master's' return. Do the players give their aid to the effort, decline the request or even attempt to sabotage the whole thing?<br /> <br /> *Both of whom are essentially 'Maxed Out' in terms of their character sheets; having every possible 'boon' (including powers and merits both 'Canon', Fan-Made and Homebrew) and maximized their Attributes and Skills.<br /> <br /> Admittedly not my best, but its twenty past midnight here, so I think that'll justify the lack of quality enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 03-06-2021, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T16:32:17-07:00","id":1440985,"title":"","content":"This was inspired by an image on post #321 on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863020-inspirational-images-for-beast/page22\">22 page of the Inspirational Images For Beast thread</a>.<br /> <br /> 105) They did it. The PC/Player Brood has walked the paths of Family, Hunger, Nightmare and Legend, and have successfully either subverted their respective heroes, spawned their own legends, dominated the region's Hive, or some combination thereof, and has finally achieved the Inheritance most commonly known as the Incarnation. They've also, most likely, created a number of Horrorspawn, and had at least a couple take on physical form. Well, here's the thing; not long after ascending, (one of) the PC(s) heads back into their lair and finds, much to their surprise, that there's still a single Horrorspawn left. But what's even <i>more</i> dumbfounding, is that the little one, upon seeing the Beast, waddles over and croaks out an unmistakable word, if somewhat garbled due to their non-human anatomy; &quot;Mama&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T11:31:47-07:00","id":1451154,"title":"","content":"106)A Talassi Beast has moved into the area, and\u2019s joined a cult of mortal alchemists. His Horror an oroboros, he preaches to his new comrades of a path to alchemical immortality. Of course, what he <i>doesn\u2019t</i> tell them is \u2018immortality\u2019 will turn them into the Thralls Lair Trait, as the Beast is ready to expand his Lair and thereby gain a new Lair Trait.<br /> The PCs get involved because one of them has Kinship with one of these alchemists!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T12:45:57-07:00","id":1451369,"title":"","content":"107)<br /> Something essential in the Hive changed. Every Beast can feel it, some sort of pulsing, hot sensation, reverberating through every Chamber. The Horrors seem drawn to it, but just can't seem to find it. Feeding seems more satiating, but at the same time substantially harder, and on top of that they grow hungry much more quickly, forcing the Begotten to up their game. At the same time, more and more Heroes appear, but who can say whether they are drawn by the pulsation, or the wildfire of careless, desperate deep Feeding?<br /> Meanwhile, someone has appeared claiming to be the Dark Mother's very own Herald. While definititely Kin and powerful, they cannot be placed among the Family the PCs know. Their cult is growing, quickly, with many <br /> If they manage to find the time in between their meals (or if they arrange a meeting with the Dark Mother's Herald after gaining enough of his trust), they can find a chamber that is not connected to any physical space, much like a Heart. A dark, visceral place, at it's center a huge mass of erratically moving flesh, the source of a high-pitched humming that is painful to bear, but instilling a sense of half-glimpsed revelations and deep truths. They just cannot shake the feeling that this is something important, that they bear witness to a monumental event - albeit catastrophic in nature. As exhausting as visiting the place is, they are drawn to it, expectant of... something. And each time the players visit, it seems to haven grow, ripened, soon ready to burst open...<br /> <br /> <br /> Will the players just wait out their time, try to put an end to this due to their feelings of foreboding doom, or try to hasten these events, in gleeful anticipation of the promised rewards?<br /> Could they even stop it if they really wanted to?<br /> What will be the consequences or repercussions when the cocoon bursts?<br /> And the most important question of all: will the Dark Mother smile upon their actions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}